  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion:sphmc-standardized-rgo-position-fisher",
    "anchor": "SPHMC arXiv2609.06906v1 S3.SS1.p1.1 eta>0, S2.E1/S3.E2/S4.Ex3 proximal and Gaussian evaluator, S4.E4/E5, Ex8/p4.1/p4.2/p4.3/E6 only lastTWO comparisons. NeighborLemma4.1 eta<=1 excluded; numericaleta<=1/(2beta) cost separate.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06906v1#S4.Ex8",
    "original_text": "Exact source component with explicit truth boundary:\nSource beta=1, alpha=kappa^-1, real kappa>=1; actual C2 V with kappa^-1*normv^2<=D2V(x)[v,v]<=normv^2 for every x,v.\nFinite real complete Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero, and arbitrary measurable parameter space S; measurable eta/y with everyeta(s)>0. These coordinate-free and parameter-space extensions are disclosed. Printed Lemma4.2 inherits eta>0 from Section3.1; the eta<=1 premise of neighboring Lemma4.1 is not consumed.\nNo supplied proximal point, law identity, normalizer, probability, curvature, gradient or moment certificate. Actual p, mu/R/r probability, normalized affine law, C2 curvature/mode and genuine position/Fisher L2 are internally produced. The numerical-prox eta<=1/(2beta) cap is a separate computational contract.\nProduce one measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. For literal rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta*inner(gradientV(p),u) and Q=normu^2/2+rho, produce C2, mode0, 0<=Hessrho<=etaI and I<=HessQ<=(1+eta)I. The actual RGO R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)) is a probability measure, and its actual standardized pushforward r equals volume.tilted(-Q). Genuine position and rho-gradient L2 satisfy integral normu^2 dr<=d and integral normgradrho^2 dr<=eta^2 integral normu^2 dr<=eta^2 d. Only the last TWO comparisons of(4.6) are covered; the first W2 comparison is open.\nAllpositive eta source3.2/4.4/4.5 plus true normalized affine posterior and lastTWO4.6 only. FIRSTW2 GaussianT2/LSI,bias4.2,centeredMGF4.3,fullLemma4.2,actual jointposterior Markov sampling/Picard/Wp/warmness/main/initialization/work/composition OPEN. Numericalprox cap eta<=1/(2beta) is separate. TV never transfers unboundedcost.",
    "text_sha256": "b63799d8109e53d12f68569705f895b290a6bfbb8d4f131d894ac7639ecc0b19"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.SmoothedPicardHMC.StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.standardized_rgo_position_and_fisher",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/SmoothedPicardHMC/StandardizedRGOPositionFisher.lean",
    "statement": "{E S : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    [MeasurableSpace S] {V : E → ℝ} {κ : ℝ}\n    (hκ : 1 ≤ κ) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, κ⁻¹*‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ∧\n      fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v v ≤ ‖v‖^2)\n    {eta : S → ℝ} {y : S → E} (heta : Measurable eta) (hy : Measurable y)\n    (hpos : ∀ s, 0 < eta s) :\n    ∃ p : S → E, Measurable p ∧\n      (∀ s, p s+eta s • gradient V (p s)=y s) ∧\n      let rho := fun s u => V (p s+Real.sqrt (eta s) • u)-V (p s)-\n        Real.sqrt (eta s)*inner ℝ (gradient V (p s)) u\n      let Q := fun s u => ‖u‖^2/2+rho s u\n      let mu := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n      let R := fun s => mu.tilted (fun x => -‖x-y s‖^2/(2*eta s))\n      let r := fun s => (R s).map (fun x => (Real.sqrt (eta s))⁻¹ • (x-p s))\n      IsProbabilityMeasure mu ∧\n        ∀ s, IsProbabilityMeasure (R s) ∧\n          ContDiff ℝ 2 (rho s) ∧ ContDiff ℝ 2 (Q s) ∧\n          gradient (rho s) 0=0 ∧ gradient (Q s) 0=0 ∧\n          (∀ u v : E, 0 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ∧\n            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (rho s)) u v v ≤ eta s*‖v‖^2) ∧\n          (∀ u v : E, ‖v‖^2 ≤ fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ∧\n            fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ (Q s)) u v v ≤ (1+eta s)*‖v‖^2) ∧\n          r s=(volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u => -Q s u) ∧\n          IsProbabilityMeasure (r s) ∧ MemLp id 2 (r s) ∧\n          Integrable (fun u => ‖u‖^2) (r s) ∧\n          (∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤ Module.finrank ℝ E ∧\n          MemLp (gradient (rho s)) 2 (r s) ∧\n          (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤\n            (eta s)^2*(∫ u, ‖u‖^2 ∂r s) ∧\n          (∫ u, ‖gradient (rho s) u‖^2 ∂r s) ≤\n            (eta s)^2*Module.finrank ℝ E",
    "statement_sha256": "0e8b91543f6056c1d0a4804d029de36ba474b3e7c2bc3091308d67ed7440a828",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "Measure.tilted mu f is mu.withDensity(x->ENNReal.ofReal(exp(f x)/(integral exp(f) dmu))). Bochner integral normalization is totalized when exponential integrability fails. Equality alone is not probability. IsProbabilityMeasure nu means nu(univ)=1.",
      "Measure.map is the genuine measurable pushforward. volume is real finite-Hilbert Lebesgue/Haar measure. Real scaling uses vector smul; finrank is the actual real dimension and may be0.",
      "ContDiff R2 and fderiv are actual twice continuous Frechet calculus. gradient f x=(InnerProductSpace.toDual R E).symm(fderiv R f x), the true real Hilbert Riesz gradient. MemLp id2r and MemLp gradientrho2r are genuine AE strong measurability and finite L2 norms.",
      "All potentials and mu/R/r are literal let bodies of the public signature. The affine identity has any F/nonzero real scale; the source theorem has actual positive-curvature V and internally produces probability, moments and gradients. No estimate-certificate aliases occur.",
      "R is the literal conditional Gibbs RGO tilt and r is its centered/sqrteta standardized pushforward. Neither is the earlier Gaussian gradient-output law nor HMC K/Khat/Kbar. Joint measurability of the posterior measure-valued family is not a conclusion."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "Actual focused3729 PASS/standard3. Two sourceAnchors preproof statement/topology independentlysealed before API/proofsearch. Generic54line affine proof unchanged; consumer-range prose only, no new proof credit."
