    "statement": "Produce one measurable exact proximal selector p satisfying p+eta*gradientV(p)=y. For literal rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta*inner(gradientV(p),u) and Q=normu^2/2+rho, produce C2, mode0, 0<=Hessrho<=etaI and I<=HessQ<=(1+eta)I. The actual RGO R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)) is a probability measure, and its actual standardized pushforward r equals volume.tilted(-Q). Genuine position and rho-gradient L2 satisfy integral normu^2 dr<=d and integral normgradrho^2 dr<=eta^2 integral normu^2 dr<=eta^2 d. Only the last TWO comparisons of(4.6) are covered; the first W2 comparison is open.",
